msgid "Using JMS"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This guide demonstrates how your Quarkus application can use JMS messaging "
"via the\n"
"Apache Qpid JMS AMQP client, or alternatively the Apache ActiveMQ Artemis "
"JMS client."
msgstr ""

msgid "This technology is considered {extension-status}."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In _preview_, backward compatibility and presence in the ecosystem is not "
"guaranteed.\n"
"Specific improvements might require changing configuration or APIs, and "
"plans to become _stable_ are under way.\n"
"Feedback is welcome on our https://groups.google.com/d/forum/quarkus-"
"dev[mailing list] or as issues in our https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"issues[GitHub issue tracker]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For a full list of possible statuses, check our https://quarkus.io/faq/#what-"
"are-the-extension-statuses[FAQ entry]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

msgid "To complete this guide, you need:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Roughly 15 minutes"
msgstr ""

msgid "An IDE"
msgstr ""

msgid "JDK 17+ installed with `JAVA_HOME` configured appropriately"
msgstr ""

msgid "Apache Maven {maven-version}"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Optionally the xref:cli-tooling.adoc[Quarkus CLI] if you want to use it"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Optionally Mandrel or GraalVM installed and xref:building-native-image."
"adoc#configuring-graalvm[configured appropriately] if you want to build a "
"native executable (or Docker if you use a native container build)"
msgstr ""

msgid "A running Artemis server, or Docker to start one"
msgstr ""

msgid "Architecture"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In this guide, we are going to generate (random) prices in one component.\n"
"These prices are written to a queue (`prices`) using a JMS client.\n"
"Another component reads from the `prices` queue and stores the latest price.\n"
"The data can be fetched from a browser using a fetch button from a Jakarta "
"REST resource."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The guide can be used either via the Apache Qpid JMS AMQP client as detailed "
"immediately below, or\n"
"alternatively with the Apache ActiveMQ Artemis JMS client given some "
"different configuration\n"
"as <<artemis-jms,detailed later>>."
msgstr ""

msgid "Qpid JMS - AMQP"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the detailed steps below we will use the https://qpid.apache.org/"
"components/jms/[Apache Qpid JMS]\n"
"client via the https://github.com/amqphub/quarkus-qpid-jms/[Quarkus Qpid JMS "
"extension]. Qpid JMS\n"
"uses the AMQP 1.0 ISO standard as its wire protocol, allowing it to be used "
"with a variety of\n"
"AMQP 1.0 servers and services such as ActiveMQ Artemis, ActiveMQ 5, Qpid "
"Broker-J, Qpid Dispatch router,\n"
"Azure Service Bus, and more."
msgstr ""

msgid "Solution"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We recommend that you follow the instructions in the next sections and "
"create the application step by step.\n"
"However, you can go right to the completed example."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Clone the Git repository: `git clone https://github.com/amqphub/quarkus-qpid-"
"jms-quickstart.git`,\n"
"or download an https://github.com/amqphub/quarkus-qpid-jms-quickstart/"
"archive/main.zip[archive]."
msgstr ""

